---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
---

<Base
  title="rowlab — Ask a question of every row"
  description="Label, extract and rewrite tabular data with AI. Compare models, inspect answers and scale from a sample to your full dataset. Open source, with an API and MCP."
>
  <div class="hero">
    <h1>Ask a question of every row.</h1>
    <p>
      rowlab labels, extracts and rewrites tabular data with AI. Add a CSV, JSON or Parquet file,
      write the question, try it on twenty rows, then run it on a million. Open source, runs on your
      laptop, or hosted when you'd rather not run it.
    </p>
    <div class="actions">
      <a class="button primary" href="https://app.rowlab.dev">Try it hosted</a>
      <a class="button" href="https://docs.rowlab.dev/get-started">Run it yourself</a>
    </div>
  </div>

  <section>
    <pre><code>uvx rowlab</code></pre>
    <p class="lead">
      One process, one SQLite file, one data folder. Open <code>localhost:8000</code>, add a file,
      and bring your own <a href="https://openrouter.ai">OpenRouter</a> key.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="columns">
    <div>
      <h3>Try before you pay</h3>
      <p>
        See the rows, calls and cost before a run. Run two models on the same rows and compare them,
        against your own labels if you have any. Cheap decision models for yes/no questions, LLMs for
        the rest.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Nothing changes in place</h3>
      <p>
        Every run makes a new dataset with the answers added, named after where it came from. Keep
        the tree, export any branch as CSV, JSONL or Parquet, to a file or S3.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div>
      <h3>Built for people and agents alike</h3>
      <p>
        A fast web app, a plain API, and an MCP server with skills that teach agents to label well.
        The same work, whichever way you do it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What a run looks like</h2>
    <p class="lead">
      Pick the rows with SQL, write the question from the row's own columns, choose the answer type,
      and a model.
    </p>
    <pre><code>SELECT * FROM data WHERE stars &lt;= 2 LIMIT 20

Is this review about delivery?
Review of a kitchen product: &#123;&#123;review&#125;&#125;

yes / no  ·  typesafe/jev-1.14  ·  20 calls  ·  $0.00</code></pre>
    <p class="lead">
      Read the answers next to the rows. Fix the prompt. Then take the <code>LIMIT</code> off.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Who it's for</h2>
    <ul class="who">
      <li><strong>Analysts</strong> with a column to fill in.</li>
      <li><strong>Teams</strong> making training data.</li>
      <li><strong>Researchers</strong> coding open-ended answers.</li>
      <li><strong>Ops</strong> triaging tickets and reviews.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Answer types</h2>
    <div class="columns">
      <div>
        <h3>Classify</h3>
        <p>
          Yes/no, pick one, pick any, or a score on a scale. Any model, each answer with its
          probability.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Extract</h3>
        <p>Typed fields pulled out of the row: text, numbers, dates, lists. Empty when the text doesn't say.</p>
      </div>
      <div>
        <h3>Write</h3>
        <p>New text from the row: a summary, a translation, a rewrite.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
